{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "pmat",
          "version": "3.42.0"
        }
      },
      "invocations": [
        {
          "executionSuccessful": true,
          "toolExecutionNotifications": []
        }
      ],
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "has-entry-awk-extra-blanks-after-colon",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "The new has_entry reader consumes exactly one blank after `release:` and never strips leading blanks from the value, so `release:  \"0.71.0\"` (two blanks, as a maintainer aligning columns would write) leaves r = ` \"0.71.0\"`, fails the quote strip and compares unequal: the entry is missed and a per-release entry could ride beside the standing policy. The header comment claims every YAML shape is matched; this one is not, and the 7 new per-release rows do not plant it. Reproduced on the real awk (rc 1, expected 0). Fix: strip leading blanks from r before the quote strip."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "scripts/lib/release_policy_has_entry.awk"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 10
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "measured",
            "command": [
              "bash",
              "-c",
              "printf '  emergency_scopes:\\n    - id: x\\n      release:  \"0.71.0\"\\n  other: 1\\n' | awk -v v=0.71.0 -f scripts/lib/release_policy_has_entry.awk; echo rc=$?"
            ],
            "exit_code": 0,
            "stdout_sha256": "91d957f8f2748a950526d4d21e0d5cd3bf5518e6c60b1beb470a13be1f978b1d",
            "failure_scenario": "A ladder edit adds an emergency_scopes entry written `release:  \"0.71.0\"` for the cut being prepared; has_entry returns 1 (no entry), so the standing policy and a per-release ruling both apply to one release, which the one-release-one-ruling rule forbids.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "rp-unq-and-known-red-ignore-inline-comments",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "rp_unq strips only an exact enclosing pair, and rp_get returns the raw value including any trailing comment. `ticket_owner: '#123' # comment` therefore reaches the owner regex with its quotes and comment and the reader refuses it with rc 2. It fails closed (no ticket is opened, the step dies with the reason), so this is a usability gap, not a pass-through; the comment-free forms the delta targets (double, single, bare) are all handled and have rows. rp_known_failures has the neighbouring gap: awk takes $2, so a ticket quoted with an interior blank (`\"#42 \"`) is cut at the blank and the leading quote is printed into the release notes. Both reproduced."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "scripts/lib/release_policy.sh"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 74
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "measured",
            "command": [
              "bash",
              "-c",
              "rp_ticket_owner on a ladder whose release_policy.ticket_owner is '#123' # comment; echo RC=$? WHY=$RP_WHY"
            ],
            "exit_code": 0,
            "stdout_sha256": "df695b469f6978a31eab362ccd291641b2eef76920d3a5543e27400e6d24c93e",
            "failure_scenario": "A maintainer comments the owner line; the nightly refuses with rc 2 and opens no ticket until the comment is removed. With a blank inside the quoted known_red ticket the release notes print `known red (ladder), \"#42`.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "search-guard-accepts-non-array-json",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "The new page check treats any output where `jq length` is a number below 50 as a readable list. `length` is also defined for an object, a string and null, so a gh reply of {\"a\":1} (length 1) or null (0) passes as an empty list and a ticket is opened. gh issue list --json always prints an array, so this needs a broken or substituted gh, and the row tickets_unreadable_search_opens_nothing plants only non-JSON text. Fix: require `type == \"array\"` before taking the length. The literal 50 appears in the command and in the check, unshared."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "scripts/release/models_nightly.sh"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 219
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "cited",
            "source": "scripts/release/models_nightly.sh",
            "excerpt": "    len=$(jq 'length' <<< \"$j\" 2> /dev/null) || len=\"\"",
            "excerpt_sha256": "0c7bd17c9637f7b2fe773d039a2fb9f2a9e816e5c0083eaa153279709361de3d",
            "failure_scenario": "MODELS_NIGHTLY_GH or a gh wrapper returns a JSON object or null; len is 1 or 0, n is empty, and a duplicate ticket is opened for a row that may already have one.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "mktemp-check-has-no-row",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "The mktemp failure is now checked on the assignment itself, which is correct: a plain assignment propagates the substitution status. No row in the 98 plants a failing mktemp (the self-test count is unchanged at 98 and the new string appears on one line only), so a regression to an unchecked mktemp would keep every row green."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "scripts/check_publish_preflight.sh"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 375
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "cited",
            "source": "scripts/check_publish_preflight.sh",
            "excerpt": "    out=\"$(mktemp)\" || { POL_WHY=\"mktemp failed, so the policy ladder could not be written\"; return 2; }",
            "excerpt_sha256": "bfbef88db5862dd1d2e93750b5834982c5d1c139f6ebd972208df40728157426",
            "failure_scenario": "The check is deleted or inverted later; with a full /tmp the ladder is written to an empty path and the redirect error is hidden, and nothing in the self-test notices.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "delta-e79344669c-verified",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Each delta item the task listed was checked rather than repeated. (1) red_rows selects green != true: a rung with no green key is now named, row tickets_rung_without_green_is_red proves it, and m30 reverts it. (2) A full (50) or unreadable search page with no title match is NOT-MEASURED (rc 2, no issue create): rows tickets_full_search_page_opens_nothing and tickets_unreadable_search_opens_nothing; the array-type gap is the advisory above. (3) rp_unq strips one matching pair of single or double quotes; a mismatched pair is left alone; rows since-single-quoted and owner-single-quoted. (4) known_red tickets strip a matching pair only. (5) has_entry matches the key in either position, any quoting, a trailing comment, and compares X.Y.Z cores; the extra-blank gap is the advisory above. (6) mktemp is checked. Measured at this head: policy self-test 55 rows 0 failed, pre-flight 98/98, models_nightly 82/82. The GH-4915 roadmap entry is identical in roadmap.yaml and entries/GH-4915.yaml. The bash mutant sets of the touched guards were run at this head: 110 of 110 killed."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "scripts/release/models_nightly.sh"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 182
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "measured",
            "command": [
              "bash",
              "scripts/release/models_nightly.sh",
              "--self-test"
            ],
            "exit_code": 0,
            "stdout_sha256": "bc1b1e25d8f9a02c1e25f9930bac895e25828e92225f6b6fbabca58ecc867c69",
            "failure_scenario": "none: the claimed behaviour holds; had the page check or the green test regressed, the named rows would be red.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "cargo-mutants",
          "version": "bash-sed-mutants"
        }
      },
      "invocations": [
        {
          "executionSuccessful": true,
          "toolExecutionNotifications": []
        }
      ],
      "results": []
    },
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "antigravity",
          "version": "1.3.1"
        }
      },
      "invocations": [
        {
          "executionSuccessful": true,
          "toolExecutionNotifications": []
        }
      ],
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "rp-unq-fails-on-spaces-and-comments",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "rp_unq quote stripping fails if the YAML value contains leading/trailing alignment spaces or inline comments, because release_policy_block.awk preserves them."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "scripts/lib/release_policy.sh"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 74
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "measured",
            "command": [
              "bash",
              "-c",
              "cat > test_ladder_spaces.yaml <<'EOF'\\n  release_policy:\\n    name: crux-smoke\\n    since: \"0.0.0\"\\n    date: \"2026-10-07\"\\n    quote: \"q\"\\n    hosts: [lambda, gx10]\\n    thinking: [\"off\", \"on\"]\\n    larger_rows: nightly\\n    red_row_needs: ticket\\n    ticket_owner: '#123' # comment\\n    release_notes: known_failures\\nEOF\\nsource scripts/lib/release_policy.sh\\nrp_ticket_owner test_ladder_spaces.yaml\\necho \"RC=$? WHY=$RP_WHY\""
            ],
            "source": "scripts/lib/release_policy.sh",
            "failure_scenario": "A maintainer adds an inline comment (e.g., `ticket_owner: '#42' # comment`) or uses multiple spaces for alignment (`since:   '0.71.0'`). Because `release_policy_block.awk` preserves these spaces and comments, the extracted string does not start or end with a quote character. `rp_unq`'s strict anchor regexes (`^\"(.*)\"$`) then fail to strip the quotes. The subsequent validations fail, and the nightly job either fails closed with no tickets opened, or the release policy is erroneously rejected.",
            "precision_class": "advisory",
            "rationale_for_class": "The antigravity arm is advisory until it has 30 measured samples; the primary reproduced the comment case on the reviewed head (rc 2, fails closed)."
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "has-entry-awk-fails-on-leading-spaces",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "release_policy_has_entry.awk fails to parse version strings with multiple leading alignment spaces due to single-space consumption in the regex."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "scripts/lib/release_policy_has_entry.awk"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 10
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "measured",
            "command": [
              "bash",
              "-c",
              "cat > test_has_entry_spaces.yaml <<'EOF'\\n  emergency_scopes:\\n    - name: test\\n      release:   '1.2.3'\\nEOF\\nawk -v v=\"1.2.3\" -f scripts/lib/release_policy_has_entry.awk test_has_entry_spaces.yaml\\necho \"RC=$?\""
            ],
            "source": "scripts/lib/release_policy_has_entry.awk",
            "failure_scenario": "If an emergency scope entry is formatted with multiple alignment spaces (e.g., `- release:   \"1.2.3\"`), the regex `/^    (- |  )release:[ ]/` consumes exactly one space. The extra spaces are retained in the extracted string `r` (e.g., `  \"1.2.3\"`). The subsequent quote stripping condition `r ~ /^\".*\"$/` fails because the string starts with a space. The version match fails, and the script falsely reports no entry, allowing a duplicate entry to be appended which violates the one-ruling-per-release rule.",
            "precision_class": "advisory",
            "rationale_for_class": "Advisory until the arm has 30 measured samples; the primary reproduced it on the real awk (rc 1, expected 0)."
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "known-failures-ticket-truncated-at-blank",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "rp_known_failures incorrectly truncates ticket values containing spaces inside quotes (due to t = $2), preventing the new quote stripping logic from matching."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "scripts/lib/release_policy.sh"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 136
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "measured",
            "command": [
              "bash",
              "-c",
              "cat > test_kf_space.yaml <<'EOF'\\n  known_red:\\n    - rung: test-rung\\n      ticket: \"#42 \"\\nEOF\\nsource scripts/lib/release_policy.sh\\nrp_known_failures test_kf_space.yaml repo"
            ],
            "source": "scripts/lib/release_policy.sh",
            "failure_scenario": "A maintainer accidentally includes a trailing space inside the quotes of a ticket (e.g., `ticket: \"#123 \"`). The awk script uses `t = $2`, which truncates the string at the space (yielding `\"#123`). The new quote stripping logic `t ~ /^\".*\"$/` fails to match because the truncated string no longer ends with a quote. The leading quote is retained and incorrectly emitted, resulting in malformed release notes like `known red (ladder), \"#123`.",
            "precision_class": "advisory",
            "rationale_for_class": "Advisory until the arm has 30 measured samples; the primary reproduced it (the release note prints the leading quote)."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
